WEBVTT

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:36.950
What's this?

00:01:43.660 --> 00:01:45.580
Hey, are you all right?!

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:47.670
You didn't hit your head?

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.330
You didn't break any bones?!

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:52.880
You look so thin.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.340
Maybe you've snapped a bone or two?

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:58.090
Well, Nii-chan?

00:01:58.090 --> 00:01:59.510
Does it hurt anywhere?

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:06.350
Are you hurt?!

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:08.940
You're the one that's hurt, you idiot!

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.650
Stop! Don't come near me!

00:02:10.650 --> 00:02:11.150
Huh?

00:02:11.560 --> 00:02:14.150
Now that you mention it, I do feel kinda—

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.530
You're making me dirty!

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:18.320
Damn it!

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:20.030
Get off!

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:25.540
Okay, that's stopped the bleeding.

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:29.000
This is made from the sap
of the Rehmannia root.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.630
It helps clot blood.

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:31.380
Is it okay?

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.630
Uh, yeah.

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.300
You should use honeysuckle to disinfect it.

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:38.930
If there are any bruises, burn some leopard plant, and stick it on the bruise.

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:41.800
These plants sacrificed themselves to cure you.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.640
So you'd better thank them.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:46.680
What?

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:47.730
Mm-hmm!

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:50.060
No doubt about it.
You say some great things!

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:50.940
I like you!

00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:55.530
But what were you doing up in that tree?

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:59.110
You're not really at an age
to climb trees for fun.

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:00.820
Obviously!

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:02.120
I'm looking for something.

00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.120
What are you looking for?

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:06.950
Ah, I know. You were trying to catch
a sparrow or something.

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:08.620
Did it run away from you?

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:11.040
If you don't mind me,
I'll give you a hand.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:13.210
Do you live around here?

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:16.880
Yeah, and I know lots of the local people.

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.380
I know what happens
around here quite well.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:21.220
Then I don't suppose you'd know...

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:24.180
whether anything strange
has happened around here.

00:03:24.180 --> 00:03:25.180
Anything strange?

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.520
Like a house fire of unknown origin,

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.980
cracks in the ground, or problems at a wood shop.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.230
Huh?

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:33.100
Those sound pretty outrageous.

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:37.570
Well, I haven't heard of anything like that from ordinary people,

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:41.780
and merchants would regard it
as a bad omen and keep it secret.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:43.820
Ah, hold on.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:45.830
Maybe that place...

00:03:45.830 --> 00:03:47.870
You remember something strange?

00:03:47.870 --> 00:03:50.410
Well, something probably happened...

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:52.830
That's fine for now. Tell me!

00:03:53.880 --> 00:03:55.460
I don't mind telling.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:04:00.340
But how does this relate to
what you're looking for?

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:03.840
Are there complicating circumstances?

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:07.430
I don't really mind.

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:12.190
But if I don't find that shop soon,
people are going to get killed there.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.410
That was impressive.

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:25.410
You're wrong!

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.240
That was snoring!

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:29.160
That's no less embarrassing.

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:34.120
There was only tofu, miso,
and rice left in the kitchen,

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.130
so this was all I could make.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.130
Here, eat.

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:43.550
No!

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:45.430
I'm busy reflecting on my sins.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:48.430
I'm being taught a lesson
through the pain of hunger!

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.850
Ah, but the savory scent of the miso...

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:55.100
No, no, stop, stop...

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:57.860
And yet you're still holding it
firmly in your hands.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:03.440
What happened to your bottomless stomach?

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.950
I said something I shouldn't have.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:12.160
I didn't need to talk to Toki
about myself, but I just...

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.540
Once you trust someone, you start telling him everything about yourself.

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:18.580
Wh-Who does?!

00:05:19.340 --> 00:05:20.920
What does it matter?

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.210
He really likes you.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:26.180
You can rely on him a little, can't you?

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:33.680
Hey, am I wrong?

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.940
I thought he was a weak person with no self-consciousness,

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:40.110
who simply followed those around him.

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:42.480
That's why I couldn't bring myself to like him.

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:48.030
But he kept getting involved in
so many things without a reason.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:50.950
He created his own way of finding his place...

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:53.950
and for other people as well.

00:05:54.540 --> 00:05:57.290
Even though he doesn't seem able to resist outside influences,

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:01.290
sometimes I see a strong core,
like a beam supporting a house.

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:08.760
He's very sensitive to the feelings of others, so he thinks before he speaks.

00:06:08.760 --> 00:06:11.800
He provides answers to people seeking them.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:15.310
So he doesn't give in to his weakness and collapse under pressure.

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:22.020
He never forgets to watch himself and just does what he needs to, without stretching himself.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:24.480
That's why he thinks ahead.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:27.360
I think it's a great secret to life.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:32.740
That's the kind of strength you felt from him.

00:06:32.740 --> 00:06:36.620
His weakness and lack of power have both been turned into courage.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:40.250
That's who Rikugou Tokidoki is.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:48.300
Well, it's a lifestyle you can never master,
because you're so impetuous and self-centered.

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:51.840
If you mock me, I won't forgive you!

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:53.300
Give me seconds!

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:55.930
You just ate a ton.

00:06:55.930 --> 00:06:57.770
What happened to repenting?

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.520
In Rousseau's words,

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.610
"We are born, so to speak, twice over:

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:04.320
First into existence,

00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:07.150
and then into life."

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:09.610
Ruso? Rusou?

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:12.570
It means that you're born
the first time just to exist,

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:16.740
and your second life starts
when you find a purpose in life.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:21.250
People like you live for the sake of living,

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:26.250
but people like Toki need a reason to live.

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:28.880
It's what you'd call a dilemma to envy.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.130
That's just unhealthy.

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:34.800
If you go for a run in the garden,
you'll feel better.

00:07:37.060 --> 00:07:39.890
People who need a reason to live...

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:42.310
People who would just feel better after a run.

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:45.770
There are all kinds of people,
so misunderstandings and collisions occur.

00:07:46.820 --> 00:07:49.990
And that's why we must
rely on one another,

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:52.200
to better understand and
then to help each other.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:54.910
Even though he was a wandering priest,

00:07:54.910 --> 00:07:58.830
that Rusou guy said things that are pretty difficult to understand.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:01.790
But anyway, this was a nice talk.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:05.540
It's "Rusou" written with the kanji for flow and priest, right?

00:08:05.540 --> 00:08:07.670
His name fits him perfectly.

00:08:07.670 --> 00:08:10.460
As expected from someone in the same occupation as Shamon-sama!

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:11.420
How admirable!

00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:14.430
Just shut up and eat.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.180
Why...

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:23.520
Why will no one save my master?

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:27.900
You damned humans!

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:32.650
And with that, we're out of tea.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.660
Empty here too.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:37.320
Really?

00:08:37.320 --> 00:08:39.200
I wanted to have some!

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:43.210
Hey, why are <i>you</i> here?!

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:46.380
Oh, did I interrupt your private time?

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:48.000
I'm so sorry.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.760
I was lured here by this amazing smell.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.050
Yeah, right.

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:55.300
You really came here just to listen to what we were talking about.

00:08:55.890 --> 00:08:59.050
As I thought, you're nothing
but a snoopy old man.

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:04.890
You knew from the start
that he wasn't normal, right?

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:09.860
Well, if I'd said something,
you two would've been on your guard.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.860
Shamon didn't approve either.

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:17.410
Of course I knew.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:21.120
I also knew that Tokidoki was the Blank Page from Higan.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:24.000
And that you're just like him too.

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:24.870
Me too?

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:25.710
Yes.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:30.460
As far as we know, you were
the first Blank Page in this era.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:31.880
But in your case,

00:09:31.880 --> 00:09:36.880
because no one came before you,
we waited to see what would happen.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:43.560
Then in a sudden surprise,
you were no longer the Blank Page.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.350
But ever since the "stranger" appeared,

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:49.650
holes have started appearing
all over heaven's net.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:52.070
You were obviously the cause.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:55.490
Ah, this is lukewarm.

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:59.530
But when we finally realized
we could use you, it was too late.

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:02.030
We found out that in the year
you'd been here...

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:06.250
you'd become useless.

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:10.840
Teiten found you and then
bound you to heaven's net,

00:10:11.130 --> 00:10:16.760
and just like for us, the time of your death
has already been decided.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:19.720
But even if we can't use you anymore,

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:23.890
there are a lot of people we <i>can</i> use,
so it doesn't matter.

00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:29.270
Princess, a medicated bath
is being prepared!

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:38.450
Shinshu-chan?

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:44.540
What's the matter?

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:47.620
The Princess...

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.290
Save the Princess.

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:53.130
Just like you saved that girl,
get rid of the curse!

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:53.670
Huh?

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:56.880
I must get rid of Ginshu-san's curse?

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:00.430
You're the only one that can save her.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:02.300
Brother!

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:04.350
Yes, yes, good girl.

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:05.720
Everything is all right now.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:08.640
The Princess has done nothing wrong.

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:10.810
The Princess protected me!

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:18.860
Hey! Shinshu!

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:24.780
It's you again?

00:11:24.780 --> 00:11:27.870
Man, how the heck do you get in here?

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.790
It's really strange that she likes us.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:34.290
Well, I'm pretty bored, so I don't mind.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:38.260
So what should we play today?

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:43.840
I don't know who they are, and they're gruff,
but they're kind too.

00:11:43.840 --> 00:11:44.640
Huh?

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:49.520
Then as your guardian,
I'd better thank them.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.020
You'll go and meet them?

00:11:51.020 --> 00:11:52.310
Of course.

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:54.060
Will you let me join you?

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:56.730
I guess I'll have to.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:11:59.690
That's where it all went wrong.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:12.370
To think you actually were <i>his</i> sister...

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:16.210
Leaving the barrier so carelessly
really was bad luck.

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:18.670
You can die together!

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:22.090
Shin... run.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:26.600
No!

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:28.600
It was my fault!

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:31.810
The Princess did nothing wrong.

00:12:31.810 --> 00:12:35.020
It was all because I was an idiot.

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.610
I fell for their trick, so it was my fault.

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:39.690
I'll accept any punishment.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:41.440
Please!

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:47.070
I have to say something.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:56.000
I understand your feelings.

00:12:56.630 --> 00:12:59.130
But I don't have the confidence.

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:10.640
Move.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:13.640
No matter how many times
I try, nothing happens.

00:13:16.850 --> 00:13:19.480
It doesn't work like it did back then.

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:22.280
I became scared,

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:24.110
because I was torn between...

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:27.360
people's expectations and my own power,

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:29.120
which I couldn't understand.

00:13:42.460 --> 00:13:44.970
I'm sorry, Shinshu-chan.

00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:47.430
It's okay. Thank you.

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:54.560
In spite of your name, you're a real crybaby.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:57.390
But even I have times when I need to cry.

00:13:58.310 --> 00:13:59.810
Don't tell that to anyone.

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:04.400
But being weak isn't necessarily a bad thing.

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:07.030
When your weak self can't do anything,

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:09.570
you need to get help from someone else,

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:12.030
whether it's an enemy or a friend.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:15.830
The rest is based on your strength.

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:21.960
When I lived in an overtly normal world,

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:24.210
I thought I couldn't do anything.

00:14:24.880 --> 00:14:27.970
But based on a single change, I thought I could do anything.

00:14:29.130 --> 00:14:32.760
High expectations from others,
and responsibilities,

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:38.020
awaited me in Amatsuki, the world
where impossible things can happen.

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:45.440
I can't use my power because of
the weak feelings I currently have.

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.360
And I need to get help from someone else.

00:14:48.360 --> 00:14:53.240
That might cause you to be frightened,

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:55.660
but I'll do something about it.

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:03.670
I have to rely on you.

00:15:03.670 --> 00:15:05.710
Please, Bonten.

00:15:12.090 --> 00:15:13.010
Princess.

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:15.470
How are you feeling?

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:19.520
If the pain is too much to bear,
perhaps it is better to return to the doll.

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:23.150
The pain is no longer terrible.

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:27.900
Although it binds me to my life, that body is a doll, after all.

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:32.320
Once I enter it, fear and pain,

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:36.490
even joy and happiness, become unreal.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:44.000
I have my life, but one day
I may no longer be myself.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:45.340
Princess.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.750
That is what I fear.

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:50.130
Please stay strong.

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:54.090
If our Princess loses faith,
what will we do?

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:56.470
It's all right, Tsuruume.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:16:02.810
For now, I can't leave that girl alone.

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:22.120
You really <i>are</i> rash.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:27.460
Since we're meeting face to face
for the first time, it's nice to meet you.

00:16:27.750 --> 00:16:28.960
I guess that's true.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:30.420
How dare you!

00:16:30.420 --> 00:16:32.170
Calling us to a place like this.

00:16:32.170 --> 00:16:33.300
Are you trying to kill us?

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:34.970
Calm down, Utsubushi.

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:37.890
But this is a surprise,

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:42.230
calling us into the middle of enemy headquarters, and even destroying the barrier.

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:43.440
Barrier?

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:44.650
What?

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:47.480
So you didn't even know
there <i>was</i> a barrier?

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:49.480
The power of the Hakutaku?

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:53.200
You should not let logic
be blinded by ignorance.

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:54.490
So?

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:56.820
What do you want, calling me out here?

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.700
I want to remove the curse on the Princess.

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.080
Tell me its cause.

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:03.080
I refuse.

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.880
Y-You liar!

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:10.590
You called me here to make
such a pointless request?

00:17:10.590 --> 00:17:13.550
I'm not your encyclopedia.

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:14.800
As I told you,

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:17.470
if you choose me,
I'll tell you everything.

00:17:17.930 --> 00:17:21.310
You haven't chosen anyone yet.

00:17:21.310 --> 00:17:24.520
If you don't choose,
I won't give you anything.

00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.690
I like this world.

00:17:27.690 --> 00:17:30.820
If you oppose me,
I won't show you any mercy.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:34.900
Shinshu-chan!

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:37.660
Idiot! All demons should just disappear!

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:38.490
I hate them!

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.740
Remove the Princess's curse, you cowards!

00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:42.700
How dare you!

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:45.710
If that thing in a priestess outfit is what you call a human,

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:48.000
then there are no monsters here.

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:51.000
From our point of view,
<i>humans</i> are the cowardly monsters.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:55.630
That's enough, Utsubushi.

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:58.840
We have other things to be doing anyway.

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:02.100
Sorry, but we'll take our leave.

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:06.770
If you wish to return to Higan,
you'll have to do better.

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:08.560
I want to go home,

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:11.440
but there are things I need
to do before that.

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.360
Oh, well.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:18.070
This one's on the house.

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:20.490
If you want to know the truth
behind the curse,

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:23.080
then all you need to do is go
where I'm about to go.

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:25.450
Bring that girl along with you.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:30.040
To Nihonbashi, where the fox is crying.

00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:33.670
If you trust me, then I'll meet you again there.

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:36.970
Once you complete what I ask you to do,

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:41.430
you'll then have to choose
between the Princess and me.

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:49.060
If you decide on the Princess, you can do whatever you want, without my help.

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:57.030
His help, huh?

00:18:57.860 --> 00:19:00.530
It's okay now. They won't come back.

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:02.950
I'm sorry for putting you through that.

00:19:04.160 --> 00:19:08.210
He doesn't look like the kind
of guy who tells cheap lies...

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:10.920
so maybe...

00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:15.840
Even if it was for Shinshu,

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:18.670
you summoned the tengu inside this barrier.

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:21.510
That was the only clue I had.

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:23.050
I'm sorry.

00:19:23.050 --> 00:19:27.600
I want to go back there, to Higan,

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:31.020
so I can't be your power forever.

00:19:32.190 --> 00:19:35.440
However, at least let me find
a way to break your curse.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:38.030
Break my curse?

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:42.240
And that's why you want to take Shinshu outside the barrier?

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:46.660
Hm, but how much can we trust them?

00:19:46.990 --> 00:19:49.290
The information came from the tengu, right?

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:52.040
What proof is there that this isn't a trap?

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:54.170
Then I will accompany them.

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:57.800
First of all, I promise to protect Shinshu.

00:19:58.170 --> 00:20:00.510
From anybody, and everything.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:03.300
Then I'll remain here.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:06.680
If by chance it <i>is</i> a trap, then I'll accept any punishment, anything you like.

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:08.890
Then there should be no complaints.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:12.890
Very well.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:15.940
We will send Tsuruume with you.

00:20:15.940 --> 00:20:17.650
Please watch over Shinshu.

00:20:17.650 --> 00:20:18.820
Princess!

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:20.780
You will leave tomorrow morning.

00:20:20.780 --> 00:20:23.110
We will prepare anything
you might need for the journey.

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:24.910
Please take care.

00:20:24.910 --> 00:20:27.370
Right! Thank you.

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:31.160
To Nihonbashi, where the fox is crying?

00:20:33.370 --> 00:20:34.920
Wait!

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:38.130
It's pointless to go this late at night!

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:39.460
Shut up!

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.130
Which way at the next corner?!

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:45.050
Right, but it'll already be closed at this hour!

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:51.520
See?

00:21:00.650 --> 00:21:03.700
Who... the hell are you?

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:05.950
Who knows?

00:21:09.910 --> 00:21:11.660
Th-That frightened me.

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:13.750
Who the— Where did you come from?

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:15.960
Are you from Amaza?

00:21:15.960 --> 00:21:17.080
Yes.

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:18.710
Where is your master?

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:23.670
When I was asked what
these silver droplets were,

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:27.470
I answered "dew" and disappeared.

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:30.430
You...

00:21:33.100 --> 00:21:34.940
I've been waiting for you.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:37.150
I knew you'd come.
